  "verbalization": "Jolkinolide C appears to interact with Neuropilin-2 through a series of intermediate targets, suggesting a complex network of molecular relationships. The evidence indicates that Jolkinolide C directly targets ME-180, which in turn is a target of both Coniferin and Preussochromone C. These intermediates ultimately lead to Neuropilin-2 as a downstream effect. This suggests that Jolkinolide C may exert its biological activity through a pathway involving ME-180, which is a key player in the signaling cascade leading to Neuropilin-2 activation. The integration of these targets highlights a potential mechanism where Jolkinolide C influences cellular processes through ME-180, which then modulates Neuropilin-2 function. The evidence supports a plausible, though indirect, link between Jolkinolide C and Neuropilin-2, emphasizing the role of ME-180 as a critical mediator in this relationship.",
